ology.com/2024/02/28/borobudurs-eco-friendly-step-upanat-sandals-for-sustainable-tourism/"},{"type":"url","url":"https://kemenpar.go.id/en/tourism-and-creative-economy-policies/upanat-sandals-inspired-by-the-reliefs-on-borobudur-temple"},{"type":"url","url":"https://www.kompas.id/artikel/en-produksi-upanat-tidak-bisa-digenjot-optimal"},{"type":"url","url":"https://destinasian.com/editorial/the-other-side-of-borobudur"},{"type":"url","url":"https://en.tempo.co/read/1554560/upanat-sandals-special-footwear-to-visit-borobudur-temple"}]}},{"id":"ws_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-6","type":"web_search_call","status":"completed","action":{"type":"search","query":"Borobudur \"visitor rules\" OR \"peraturan pengunjung\" OR \"kebijakan\" OR \"wajib\" sandals OR upanat OR footwear 2024 OR 2025","sources":[]}},{"id":"tco_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-5","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","status":"completed"},{"id":"tco_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-4","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","status":"completed"},{"id":"tco_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-6","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","status":"completed"},{"id":"ws_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-7","type":"web_search_call","status":"completed","action":{"type":"open_page","url":"https://www.kompas.id/artikel/en-produksi-upanat-tidak-bisa-digenjot-optimal"}},{"id":"ws_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-8","type":"web_search_call","status":"completed","action":{"type":"search","query":"Borobudur Upanat mandatory OR required OR policy 2024 OR 2025 OR 2026","sources":[]}},{"id":"tco_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-8","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","status":"completed"},{"id":"tco_4091098d-69c1-9201-9708-9be3508e6d90_call-f0185732-38db-4bf6-929c-79202449a9c4-7","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","status":"completed"},{"content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"{\n  \"points\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Upanat production capacity reaches more than 4,000 sandals per day as of early 2024, exceeding daily demand.\",\n      \"source_name\": \"Kompas.id\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.kompas.id/artikel/en-produksi-upanat-tidak-bisa-digenjot-optimal\",\n      \"date\": \"April 2, 2024\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Production managed by BUMDesma Borobudur Manunggaling Roso involving 45 craftsmen from BUMDes in 20 villages in Borobudur District, each assisted by 5-10 workers.\",\n      \"source_name\": \"Kompas.id\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.kompas.id/artikel/en-produksi-upanat-tidak-bisa-digenjot-optimal\",\n      \"date\": \"April 2, 2024\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Borobudur Temple climbing limited to maximum 1,200 visitors per day (even during peak holidays like Eid), who receive upanat sandals; demand typically 1,200 on weekends and 300-500 on regular days.\",\n      \"source_name\": \"Kompas.id\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.kompas.id/artikel/en-produksi-upanat-tidak-bisa-digenjot-optimal\",\n      \"date\": \"April 2, 2024\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Upanat sandals are woven from a combination of pandan leaves, coconut shells, and an eva sponge sheet.\",\n      \"source_name\": \"Southeast Asian Archaeology\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.southeastasianarchaeology.com/2024/02/28/borobudurs-eco-friendly-step-upanat-sandals-for-sustainable-tourism/\",\n      \"date\": \"February 28, 2024\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","logprobs":[],"annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://destinasian.com/editorial/the-other-side-of-borobudur","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"title":"https://destinasian.com/editorial/the-other-side-of-borobudur"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Injourney_Destination_Management","start_index":0,"end_index":0,